From: Prævit <software@praevit.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Do not log from set_dll_path().

set_dll_path() runs from __wine_main() before the thread's TEB exists.
TRACE() with debugstr_a() there writes the debug string through the
uninitialized thread data, corrupting process memory (seen as a crash in
setvbuf()/flockfile() or later in dyld's dlsym() on macOS 27) whenever
D3DMETAL_RUNTIME_DIR points at a real D3DMetal runtime. Upstream Wine does
not log from init_paths() for this reason.

diff -ruN a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -323,10 +323,6 @@
     for (i = 0; i < count; i++) dll_path_maxlen = max( dll_path_maxlen, strlen(dll_paths[i]) );
     dll_paths[count] = NULL;
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__x86_64__)
-    if (d3dmetal_path)
-        TRACE( "D3DMetal backend prepended DLL path %s\n", debugstr_a(d3dmetal_path) );
-#endif
 }
 
 
